## Axios API client — `src/lib/api-client.ts` (NEW)

Single axios instance. Base URL from `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` (add `apps/dashboard/.env` with `VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000` and `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` / `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`; add a `vite-env.d.ts` `ImportMetaEnv` interface for type-safety). The Supabase token is read at REQUEST time from the supabase client (not from a stale closure), so it always sends the freshest (auto-refreshed) JWT.

```ts
import axios, { AxiosError } from 'axios'
import { supabase } from './supabase'

export const apiClient = axios.create({
  baseURL: import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL,
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
})

// REQUEST: inject Supabase access token. getSession() returns the cached,
// already-refreshed session synchronously from memory in the common case.
apiClient.interceptors.request.use(async (config) => {
  const { data } = await supabase.auth.getSession()
  const token = data.session?.access_token
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`
  return config
})

// RESPONSE: on 401, sign out + hard-redirect to /login (preserving return path).
// Use window.location (not useNavigate) because interceptors live outside React.
apiClient.interceptors.response.use(
  (res) => res,
  async (error: AxiosError) => {
    if (error.response?.status === 401 && !window.location.pathname.startsWith('/login')) {
      await supabase.auth.signOut()
      const returnTo = encodeURIComponent(window.location.pathname + window.location.search)
      window.location.assign(`/login?returnTo=${returnTo}`)
    }
    return Promise.reject(error)
  },
)
```

Notes: avoid an axios redirect loop by skipping the redirect when already on `/login`. The backend Fastify JWT middleware returns 401 for missing/expired/invalid tokens; this interceptor is the single client-side handler. The active branch header is added by a SECOND request interceptor described in `branchContext` (keep the two interceptors in this same file so order is explicit). The existing `useAuthStore.logout()` should also be called inside the supabase `onAuthStateChange` handler (see `supabaseClient`) so the store clears on this 401-triggered signOut too.

