## Supabase client + session→store bridge

First: `bun add @supabase/supabase-js` IN `apps/dashboard` — it is currently only a backend dependency, NOT in the dashboard `package.json`.

### `src/lib/supabase.ts` (NEW)
```ts
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'
export const supabase = createClient(
  import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL,
  import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY,
  { auth: { persistSession: true, autoRefreshToken: true, detectSessionInUrl: true } },
)
```
`persistSession: true` makes supabase-js own token persistence in `localStorage` — so on refresh the session rehydrates automatically and the existing `useAuthStore` does NOT need its own persist middleware for tokens. The store stays a derived in-memory mirror.

### `src/features/auth/services/index.ts` (REPLACES `export {}`)
Thin wrappers over `supabase.auth`:
```ts
export const authService = {
  signIn: (email, password) => supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password }),
  signUp: (email, password) => supabase.auth.signUp({ email, password }),
  signOut: () => supabase.auth.signOut(),
  resetPassword: (email) => supabase.auth.resetPasswordForEmail(email),
  getSession: () => supabase.auth.getSession(),
}
```

### `src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx` (NEW) — the bridge
Mount ONCE near the app root (wrap inside `Providers`, see `authGuard`). It (1) hydrates the store from the existing session on mount, and (2) subscribes to `onAuthStateChange` so SIGNED_IN / SIGNED_OUT / TOKEN_REFRESHED keep the EXISTING `useAuthStore` in sync. It maps the Supabase `User` → the store's `User` shape (`{ id, email, name, avatar?, createdAt }`), pulling `name`/`avatar` from `user.user_metadata`.

```ts
function mapUser(u: SupabaseUser): User {
  return {
    id: u.id, email: u.email ?? '',
    name: u.user_metadata?.name ?? u.email?.split('@')[0] ?? '',
    avatar: u.user_metadata?.avatar_url,
    createdAt: u.created_at,
  }
}
// in effect:
supabase.auth.getSession().then(({ data }) =>
  setUser(data.session ? mapUser(data.session.user) : null))
const { data: sub } = supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange((_e, session) => {
  setUser(session ? mapUser(session.user) : null)
  if (!session) queryClient.clear()   // drop cached PHI on logout
})
return () => sub.subscription.unsubscribe()
```
Add an `isLoading` boolean to the provider (true until the first `getSession()` resolves) so the guard can show a spinner instead of bouncing a logged-in user to /login on a hard refresh. The existing `useAuthStore` interface (`user`, `isAuthenticated`, `setUser`, `logout`) is reused AS-IS — `setUser(null)` already flips `isAuthenticated` false. The `LoginForm` calls `authService.signIn`; on success the listener populates the store and the form navigates to `returnTo` (default `/`).
